@node "Req" "Requirements"
@toc "Req"

       Any Amiga (500,600,1000,1200,2000,3000,4000,4000T,5000(?)....
                  Installed S-Express, /X 2.xx or 3.xx
                         An installed AREXX


                            @{" BACK TO MAIN MENU? " link "MAIN"}

@endnode
@node "Inst" "Installation - PeiTSch dEN SueSs-Op V0.8743874"
@toc "Inst"

Just copy the files
                     @{"STARTCHAT1.txt" link "Chat1"}  
                     @{"STARTCHAT2.txt" link "Chat2"}   
                     @{"STARTCHAT3.txt" link "Chat3"}

                   to DOORS:MUICHAT/
-------------------------------------------------------
/X 2.xx or S-Express:

Edit Your SYS.CMD and snap in the following:

*CST      RM255DOORS:MUICHAT/MUICHAT.REXX
-------------------------------------------------------
/X 3.xx

go and fizzle with your bloody icons!
-------------------------------------------------------
then edit your BBS:NODEx/STARTCHAT.TXT
       or your BBS:BBSTEXTS/STARTCHAT.TXT

insert the following line at the start of this text:

~CST

                            @{" BACK TO MAIN MENU? " link "MAIN"}

@endnode
@node "Disc" "---> What it does: <---"
@toc "Disc"

If somebody tries to page you, you`ll be able to answer his chat-request
by simply pressing F1 .... (like ever before)

then, the BBS will display the BBS:NODEx/STARTCHAT.TXT (also nothing new)

In this moment, it will start the MUI-CHAT door via MCI-command (the ~)!

At this moment, the sysop on the console sees a menu where he can choose
which startchat.txt (in DOORS:MUICHAT/) he wants to be displayed!

So... you can choose up to free different startchat.txt`s NOW!

I wrote this tool, cause my girlfriend often wants to chat, and was always
abused on my name standing at the top ....



@{" Wow !" link "MAIN"}
@endnode
